{
  "id": "spme",
  "title": {
    "ja": "Bスプラインsmooth PMEの格子・次数収束",
    "en": "Mesh/order convergence of B-spline smooth PME"
  },
  "method_ids": [
    "pme",
    "spme"
  ],
  "summary": {
    "ja": "電荷をBスプラインで格子へ割り当て、FFTでEwald逆空間項を評価するsmooth PME（SPME）の小規模例です。",
    "en": "A small smooth-PME example assigns charge with B-splines and evaluates the Ewald reciprocal contribution by FFT."
  },
  "assumptions": {
    "ja": "Ewaldと同じ中性立方セルと実空間項を使います。PME族のうちEssmannらのBスプライン変種を採用し、Dardenらの原法のLagrange補間とは区別します。",
    "en": "The neutral cubic cell and real-space term match the Ewald example. The adopted PME-family variant uses Essmann-type B-splines, distinct from Darden’s original Lagrange interpolation."
  },
  "algorithm": {
    "ja": "4次または6次のcardinal Bスプラインのテンソル積で電荷を格子化し、節点スプラインの離散構造因子補正、Gaussian Green関数、3次元FFTを組み合わせます。格子エネルギーを重みの位置微分で解析的に微分します。",
    "en": "Tensor-product cardinal splines of order four or six spread the charges. Apply the nodal-spline discrete structure-factor correction and Gaussian Green function through 3D FFTs; analytically differentiate assignment weights for forces."
  },
  "validation": {
    "ja": "16³・24³・40³格子と2つの次数で、直接Ewald逆空間和との差を記録します。Ewaldと実空間項・自己項を共有する部分も明示。最細格子の力はエネルギー差分とも比較し、全電荷の保持を確認します。",
    "en": "Meshes 16³/24³/40³ and two orders are compared with directly summed Ewald reciprocal terms. Shared real/self terms are stated. Check finest-grid force derivatives by energy differences and verify assigned total charge."
  },
  "limits": {
    "ja": "有限格子のaliasingにより、エネルギー勾配型の合力は厳密にはゼロでなく、その診断量を保存します。運動量保存・長時間MD・原法PME・最適化P³M・スラブ補正の検証ではありません。",
    "en": "Finite-mesh aliasing permits nonzero net force for this energy-gradient variant; that diagnostic is reported. No exact momentum conservation, long MD, original PME, optimized P³M or slab validation is claimed."
  },
  "equations": [
    "Q_{\\mathbf j}=\\sum_iq_i\\prod_{a=1}^3M_p(u_{ia}-j_a+p/2)",
    "\\mathbf F_i=-\\partial E_h/\\partial\\mathbf r_i"
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "id": "darden1993",
      "author": "T. Darden, D. York and L. Pedersen",
      "year": 1993,
      "title": "Particle mesh Ewald: An N·log(N) method for Ewald sums in large systems",
